<title>JAPAN: Japan Nov industrial output down revised 1.4 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan Nov industrial output down revised 1.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's industrial production fell a revised 1.4 percent in November against the previous month, compared with a preliminary estimate of a 1.9 percent drop, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>A breakdown of the figures follows:</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted month on month (in pct), index base 1990:</p>
<p>			  NOV     PRELIM   MONTH AGO  NOV INDEX</p>
<p> Output		 -1.4    -1.9   +3.9	100.1</p>
<p> Shipments	    -0.5    -0.8   +3.7	102.5</p>
<p> Inventories	  -0.9    -0.9   +0.7	107.4</p>
<p>Inventories to</p>
<p> Shipments ratio    +1.4    +1.3   -4.0	112.8</p>
<p>Unadjusted year on year (in pct):</p>
<p>				   NOV	PRELIM     MONTH AGO</p>
<p> Output			  +4.5     +4.0	+6.5</p>
<p> Shipments		     +5.4     +5.1	+6.8</p>
<p> Inventories		   -0.7     -0.7	-0.1</p>
<p>Inventories to</p>
<p> Shipments ratio	     -4.0     -4.1	-5.7</p>
</text>
